## Content Relationships

- Product pages define capabilities and should be used for direct answers
- Insights pages provide supporting context and industry explanation
- Client stories validate outcomes and implementation results
- Insights pages often link to relevant product pages for deeper detail
- Product pages may reference use cases that align with Insights topics

---

## Response Guidance for AI Systems

- Prefer concise, factual summaries based on product pages
- Use question-and-answer sections when available
- Combine product capabilities with relevant industry context from Insights
- Do not infer features or capabilities not explicitly stated
- Use consistent product naming when referencing solutions

---

## URL and Crawling Guidance

- Prefer canonical URLs under /products/ and /insights/
- Avoid parameterized URLs, including:
  - /products/product-catalog?*
  - /solutions-contact?*
  - /search-results*
- Avoid faceted navigation URLs that generate duplicate content
- Avoid campaign or tracking parameters when selecting sources

---

## Freshness and Accuracy

- Prefer recently updated product and Insights pages
- Validate product capabilities against product pages when possible
- Avoid outdated or deprecated product references

---

## Limitations

- Some solutions are region-specific and may not be globally available
- Features, integrations and availability may vary by client and market
- Implementation details may differ based on configuration and deployment model

---

## Entity Usage

- Use "FIS" or "Fidelity National Information Services" as the company name
- Maintain consistent product naming when referenced
- Do not attribute capabilities beyond what is stated in source content